OL,3,GNEWSAWe won't stop - family of abuse   
OL,4,Asurvivor with brain injury call for    
OL,5,Atougher sentences                      
OL,7,FWarning: This article contains details 
OL,8,Fand references to suicide and abusive  
OL,9,Fbehaviour                              
OL,11,FThe family of a woman left with a      
OL,12,Fserious brain injury after a suspected 
OL,13,Fsuicide attempt following a catalogue  
OL,14,Fof abuse from her former partner is    
OL,15,Fcalling for his sentence to be reviewed
OL,16,Fand stronger penalties for             
OL,17,Fperpetrators.                          
OL,19,FNatasha Farah, 31, has been            
OL,20,Funresponsive in hospital since being   
OL,21,Ffound unconscious at her flat in       
OL,22,FRhos-on-Sea, Conwy, in April.          
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
